  "reasoning": "The patient reports a frequent urge to urinate, pain during urination (dysuria), cloudy urine, and strong-smelling urine. These are classic clinical hallmarks of a urinary tract infection (UTI). While diabetes can cause frequent urination, it does not typically present with dysuria, cloudy appearance, or foul odor, which effectively rules it out. The combination of irritative voiding symptoms and abnormal urine characteristics firmly establishes urinary tract infection as the correct diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]urinary tract infection[/DIAGNOSIS]"
